---
const mediaBase = "https://cdn.hob.farm/articles/sharksploitation";
---

<figure class="mondo-sequence article-wide not-prose">
  <div class="mondo-sequence__grid">
    <img
      src={`${mediaBase}/mondo-cane1.png`}
      alt="Men work beside fishing nets, boats, and timbers on a beach in a frame from Mondo Cane."
      width="720"
      height="540"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      data-lightbox={`${mediaBase}/mondo-cane1.png`}
      data-lightbox-caption="The sequence first supplies a beach and a community framed by the narrator as victims."
    />
    <img
      src={`${mediaBase}/mondo-cane2.png`}
      alt="A woman handles fishing net on the same beach in a frame from Mondo Cane."
      width="720"
      height="540"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      data-lightbox={`${mediaBase}/mondo-cane2.png`}
      data-lightbox-caption="The sequence turns daily work into evidence for a story the voice-over has already decided."
    />
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Frames from <cite>Mondo Cane</cite> (1962), used in direct criticism of the film’s construction. The narration makes the accusations; the images do not independently prove them.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .mondo-sequence {
    margin-block: 2.75rem;
  }

  .mondo-sequence__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.55rem;
    padding: 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid rgb(119 167 177 / 0.34);
    background: #061417;
  }

  .mondo-sequence img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .mondo-sequence figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-base-400, #a1a1a1);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .mondo-sequence__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
